{
  // Ownship camera rig. id = CIGI view ID; gimbal = CIGI articulated part (100 + id) on entity 0.
  // mount: body FRD meters (x forward, y right, z down) relative to the ownship entity origin.
  //        yawDeg/pitchDeg/rollDeg orient the mount (pitchDeg = -90 would make gimbal (0,0) look straight down).
  // Gimbal angles are relative to the mount; see the per-rig description below and docs/ICD.md.
  // LATERAL rig: at gimbal (0,0) each camera looks horizontally out its side of the aircraft.
  //   mount yawDeg -90 = left side, +90 = right side (pitch 0). Image up = aircraft up; left cameras have the nose
  //   on image right, right cameras have the tail on image right.
  //   +elevation = up. +azimuth = clockwise seen from above: toward the NOSE for left cameras, toward the TAIL for right.
  // Mounts measured on models/aircraft/glb/b777_united.glb (scale 5.7, origin = fuselage centerline at the wing root):
  //   fore: fuselage sides at maximum breadth (skin radius 3.09 m), 18 m ahead of the origin, centerline height
  //   aft:  horizontal stabilizer tips (semi-span 11.2 m, tip chord x -37.1..-39.5, 1.9 m above the centerline)
  "cameras": [
